The voice worker's tests.

Run them from the repo root:

    python -m unittest discover -s voice/tests -t voice/tests

Nothing here needs weights, a GPU or a model download: `test_worker.py` loads
`voice/worker.py` by path and stands it up on a loopback port with a stub in
place of Kokoro and faster-whisper. Only `numpy` and `soundfile` (the worker's
own module-level imports) have to be importable.

What is covered, and why each one matters to the TypeScript side:

  the bearer gate       /speak, /stats and /audio refuse without it, and with
                        a wrong token of the same length; /health stays open,
                        because the cabinet's liveness probe leans on that
  the body cap          an over-long POST is refused on its content-length,
                        before the body is read
  the authored ranges   preset, rate, loudness, max_gap_s and the kind/preset
                        lengths are the bounds personas.json is written to
  the take              audio is served only when the receipt beside it says
                        ok, and a take id is the twenty hex characters
                        `line_id()` mints and nothing else
  the cache             the oldest take is evicted with its audio at the cap,
                        and a cached failed receipt is never re-rendered
  the accept path       a handler timeout, HTTP/1.0, daemon threads and a cap
                        on the sockets in flight — the bearer gate runs after
                        a thread is spawned, so it cannot protect this
  the cast hint         the ASR's vocabulary hint is read from the persona
                        sheets, so a new boss cannot fall out of step with it

These are not wired into CI here: the workflow files are outside this
directory's scope.
